 "description": "The right gearbox's input torque_peak is written as 0.225 kgf*cm, the 30:1 motor's 0.45 kgf*cm split in half as if two gearboxes shared one motor. Each motor drives its own gearbox, so the right gearbox receives the full 0.45 kgf*cm (0.0441 N*m) from electrical.motor_right, as the left gearbox does. As written, the torque the motor delivers and the torque the gearbox takes in do not balance at the shaft.",
